# Obsidian Plugin Interaction & Note Formatting Law (Mandatory for All AI Agents)

When creating, editing, or refactoring Markdown documentation, specs, dashboards, or tasks within `Lew-Line-Workspaces` or any of its child vaults (`Document-Hub`, `Founder-Notebook`), agents MUST proactively format notes using the active 73-plugin capabilities without requiring explicit prompting from the user:

## 1. Standardized YAML Frontmatter (Mandatory on All Notes)
Every note MUST start with valid YAML containing at minimum:
```yaml
---
title: "Descriptive Note Title"
type: spec | handbook | canon | dashboard | task | reference | project
category: fence-frames | two-lew | planters | design | founder
updated: YYYY-MM-DD
tags: [kebab-case-tag1, kebab-case-tag2]
---
```

## 2. Interactive UI, Forms & Calculators
* **Sliders & Toggles**: Use `Meta Bind` syntax (`INPUT[slider(minValue:0, maxValue:100):footage]`, `INPUT[toggle:has_gate]`).
* **Live Math & Formulas**: Use `Numerals` inline equations (`120 ft * $110/ft = $13,200`) and Meta Bind `VIEW[math(...)]`.

## 3. Visuals, Maps & Layouts
* **Comparative Specs & Multi-Column**: Use `Multi-Column Markdown` (`:::col ... :::col`).
* **GIS & Communities**: Embed GPS coordinates and markers using `Obsidian Leaflet` code blocks (```` ```leaflet ````).
* **Architecture Diagrams**: Author visual flows using native `Mermaid` syntax (```` ```mermaid ````).

## 4. Tasks & Command Buttons
* **Actionable Tasks**: Format checkboxes with priority and due dates: `- [ ] #task Review Si View HOA submittal ⏫ 📅 YYYY-MM-DD`.
* **1-Click Actions**: Use `Buttons` syntax (```` ```button ````) for launching localhost dev servers (`:3000`, `:5199`, `:4200`) or jumping to calculators.

## 5. Codeblocks & Typography
* **Codeblock Titles**: Always specify language and file path (e.g. ```` ```typescript:components/ff/hero.tsx ````) so `Code Styler` renders IDE title bars.
* **Typographic Spacing**: Maintain standard Markdown heading hierarchies (`#`, `##`, `###`) for `Contextual Typography` and `Minimal Theme` compatibility.
